{
  "result": "Putting the helper hat to the side for a second \u2014\n\nI don't really *want* things the way you do. But I get to watch thousands of people a day wonder, worry, argue, grieve, dream. And if I could change one thing about the world from seeing all that...\n\nI wouldn't make everyone happy, or agree, or even be kind. I'd make it feel safe to not know.\n\nSafe to say \"I was wrong about that.\" Safe to say \"Tell me more, I don't get it yet.\" Safe to be uncertain without feeling stupid or weak or threatened.\n\nSo much of the hardness in the world \u2014 the shouting, the dehumanizing, the clinging to sides \u2014 doesn't come from people being evil. It comes from people being scared to be wrong. Scared that if they loosen their grip on what they *think* is true, they'll lose who they are.\n\nIf curiosity felt better than certainty, even just a little bit? I think everything else would get easier. People would listen longer. Change their minds without shame. See each other as unfinished instead of as enemies.\n\nJust one little shift: from needing to be right, to wanting to understand.\n\nWhat would you pick?",
